`unseal` works on macOS, on Linux arm64, and on Linux without `/proc`. It handed gpg a `/proc/self/fd/<n>/` path to write, and opened directories with the x86-64 Linux values of `O_NOFOLLOW` and `O_DIRECTORY`; on arm64 those numbers are `O_LARGEFILE` and `O_DIRECT`, so the walk followed a directory symlink. The flags now come from `<fcntl.h>`. gpg and age write the plaintext to a pipe, and `unseal` copies it into a staging file it created with `O_CREAT|O_EXCL|O_NOFOLLOW`, mode 0600. CI runs the suite on Linux arm64 and macOS.
